  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "tonyd2wild's boot-fixed jasl sparkrun recipe for the original DeepSeek-V4-Flash on two Sparks: vLLM tensor parallel 2 on scitrera's public jasl-ds4 image (vLLM 0.22.1-jasl-ds4+21a54ea, tag 20260609, digest-pinned, used unmodified), FP8 KV cache, DeepSeek MTP with two drafted tokens, instanttensor loading, a 256,000-token context and jasl's sparse-MLA long-context chunk profile. Upstream states this is a boot fix, not a performance upgrade: it did not beat aidendle94's production-ready image on decode or long prefill on its cluster (43.8 versus 45.1 tok/s decode; 33K prefill 37.1 versus 28.0 s). Same-creator alternative for this model and Spark count: the MTP recipe on the aidendle94 image. Licences (information only): model MIT; the upstream repository declares no licence file; vLLM Apache-2.0. Upstream figures (43.8 tok/s, 79 to 85 percent MTP acceptance) are claims until measured here; Vonk physical two-Spark acceptance is pending.",
    "tags": [
      "deepseek",
      "distributed",
      "fp8-kv",
      "jasl",
      "mtp",
      "reasoning",
      "spark",
      "tool-use",
      "vllm"
    ],
    "title": "DeepSeek V4 Flash jasl vLLM two Sparks (tonyd2wild)"
  },
